{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>It crashes down</b> — it has no cognate, and the meaning is: like a weapon." "<b>At the shaking of a spear</b> — for the practice of the one holding it is to shake it."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "I read תותח as the lemma from Job 41:21, though the standard MT has תתחמץ at 41:22 (Heb verse numbering); Ibn Ezra's lemma may reflect a variant or a truncated citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:39.838262491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}